ation Deadline Tuesday, November 3rd Norton Middle School 215 West Main St. 7:00AM - 8:00PM Saturday, October 24th Tuesday, October 27th at 5:00PM Deadline to register to vote for the November 3, 2026 State Election is Saturday, October 24th. The Town Clerk's Office will be open 9:00AM - 5:00PM. Please use entrance on the left of the Fire station to access Town Hall parking lot. First row of parking spots in the \"employee parking lot\" will be reserved for those registering to vote.  Early Voting In Person  Location - Norton Town Hall, 72 East Main St., Crane Room \n \n \n \n Day Date Hours Saturday October 17 9:00AM - 3:00PM Monday October 19 9:00AM - 1:00PM Tuesday  October 20 9:00AM - 1:00PM Wednesday  October 21 9:00AM - 1:00PM Thursday October 22 9:00AM - 3:00PM Friday October 23 9:00AM - 11:00AM Sunday October 25 9:00AM - 3:00PM Monday October 26 8:30AM - 4:30PM Tuesday October 27 8:30AM - 4:30PM Wednesday October 28 8:30AM - 4:30PM Thursday October 29 8:30AM - 7:30PM Friday October 30 8:30AM - 12:30PM Sample Ballots Precincts 1 & 2 Precincts 3, 4 & 5 Notice of Advanced Removal of Early Voted Ballots from Envelopes  ( Link  provided if applicable) Agendas and Minutes Agendas are available prior to the meetings. Minutes are available following approval. View Most Recent Agendas and Minutes Town Meeting Annual Fall Town Meeting will be held Monday, October 19, 2026 at 7:00 pm at Norton High School.  The last day to register to vote for the Annual Fall Town Meeting is Friday, October 9, 2026. The Town Clerk's Office will be open 8:30am - 5:00pm to receive voter registrations or you are able to register to vote online at the following link:  Online Voter Application Mission Statement The Norton Town Clerk's Office is committed to providing courteous, competent, and efficient customer service. We are dedicated to thoroughly preserving the town's vital records and historical documents for the benefit of future generations. Our office operates in a modern, professional, and automated environment, emphasizing our fiscal responsibility to Norton's taxpayers. For general inquiries, please  email the Town Clerk's Office . View the  Code of Conduct Policy  for Appointed and Elected Board/Committee Members. \r\n     \r\n\r\n \r\n\t$(document).ready(function (e) {\t\t\r\n\t    renderSlideshowIfApplicable($('#divEditor' + '70e36c51-5407-468f-963c-c77266ded755'));\r\n\t});\r\n \r\n \r\n\n\t   \r\n\r\n\t   \r\n\r\n\t\t\t   \r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t \r\n\r\n\t \r\n\r\n\t\r\n\t \r\n\r\n\t \r\n \r\n \t \r\n\t\t\t\t                \r\n\r\n\t\t \r\t\t\t\t\n\t \r\r\n\t\n\t \r\t\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\t \r\n\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Contact Us \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t \r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t\tMelissa J. McGuinness\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t Town Clerk \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t Email  \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t\t More Information \r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t \r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t\tSamantha Rego\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t Assistant Town Clerk \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t Email  \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t\t More Information \r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t \r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t\tSarah D'Andrea\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t Election Support \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t\t More Information \r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t \r\n\t\t \r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t Town Clerk \r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t\t Email the Town Clerk's Office \r\n\t\t\t\t\t \r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Physical Address \r\n\t\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t\t 72 East Main Street \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t 1st Floor, Room 135  \r\n\t\t\t\t\t Norton ,  MA   02766 \r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t Phone:  508-285-0230 \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t Fax: 508-285-0231  \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \r\n\r\n\r\n\t\t\t\t Directory \r\n\t\t\t\t \r\n\r\n\t\t \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t \r\n\t \r\n \n\t   \r\n\r\n\t   \r\n\r\n\t\t\t   \r\n\t\t \r\t\t\t\t\n\t \r\r\n\t\n\t \r\t\r\n\t \n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\t \r\n\t\t\t \r\n\t\t \r